# PHASE 2 — COMPLETE EGYPT LOCALIZATION

The website currently presents Bangkok as its location. Replace this localization with Egypt consistently throughout the entire website.

This is not just a text replacement.

Inspect all content and location-dependent functionality, including:

- Page titles and descriptions.
- Locations and destinations.
- Addresses and geographical information.
- Maps, pins, and coordinates.
- Navigation labels.
- Search and filter options.
- Item descriptions.
- Booking details.
- Contact information.
- Currency and pricing.
- SEO metadata.
- Image captions and alternative text.
- Structured data and configuration files.

Remove outdated Bangkok-specific information wherever it is no longer relevant.

### 2.1 Use real Egyptian locations

Use genuine Egyptian destinations, places, and locations relevant to the website's existing purpose.

Verify that every displayed location actually exists and that its description accurately represents it.

Do not use random Egyptian names or imaginary destinations.

### 2.2 Replace every image with genuine Egyptian photography

This is a mandatory requirement.

Replace all Bangkok-related images and any unsuitable existing imagery with real, visually attractive photographs taken in Egypt.

Image requirements:

- Must depict actual Egyptian places, landscapes, architecture, activities, or relevant subjects.
- Must come from genuine photographic sources.
- Must not be AI-generated.
- Must not be artificial-looking or heavily manipulated.
- Must not depict another country while being presented as Egypt.
- Must be visually high quality and appropriate for the particular page or item.
- Must not repeatedly reuse the same image across different items.
- Must be optimized for fast loading without unnecessary quality loss.

Use trustworthy sources such as:
- Wikimedia Commons.
- Unsplash.
- Pexels.
- Official Egyptian tourism sources.
- Other verifiable photographic sources with appropriate usage rights.

For every image, verify its source and relevance.

Preserve attribution and licensing information wherever required.

Maintain a clear mapping between each image, its source, and the website item using it.

**Never generate replacement images with an AI image generator. Use actual photographs.**

